spans.s:
√tul (toláyati; tolayā́m āsa; tolayiṣyáti;
[]
tolitá; -tólya). --1. raise up;
 —2. esp.
raise up a thing so as to find its weight;
weigh;
 —3. counterpoise;
 —4. equal.
[orig. mg, ‘bear, i. e. hold up’: in the cognates,
 the mg ‘bear, i. e. endure’ appears:
cf. Lat. tul-i, ‘endured’; Goth. ϸul-an,
Eng. thole, ‘endure’; Ger. Ge-dul-d, ‘endurance’;
 also ἔ-τλη-ν, ‘bore,’ πολύ-τλᾱ-ς,
‘much enduring’; Lat. lātus, *tlā-tus,
‘borne.’]
